and thread repair, electrical, plugs, and wheel parts. It also provides fuses, breakers, and switches; cables and wires; grommets; light bulbs and indicators; sockets and adaptors; engraving products; fasteners, including anchors, bolts, drill bits, hurricanes, nails, pins, rings, rivets, screws, sockets, spacers, staples, threaded inserts and rods, ties, tools/brushes, washers, wire hardware, and wood parts; and fluid flow components. In addition, the company offers hardware products comprising connections, caps and plugs, door and windows, fences, garage doors, gates, household, interiors, knobs and handles, magnets, rail, gangers, reinforcements, security, shims and wedges, and springs products; key accessories; markers/reflectors, numbers, letters, plaques, signs, stencils, survey and flagging tapes; fittings, connectors, torches, and burners liquefied petroleum gas products; and wall hangings consists of adhesives, frame hardware, hooks, kits, mirror, picture hanging, tool-free mounting, and wall hanging accessories. Further, it provides plumbing products; power tool accessories; rods, shapes, and sheets; and safety and security products. It offers its products under the Power Pro, All Points, OOK, Hardware Essentials, Fastening Systems, Paulin, The Steel Works, Deck Plus, Grease Monkey, Firm Grip, Magnifeye, True Grip, AWP, Shaded Eye, McGuire-Nicholas, Gorilla Grip, intex, Axxess+, resharp, minuteokay, OTR, Digz, Fas-n-Tite, Ozco, High & Mighty, Premium Defense, Keykrafter, KeyHero, Quick-Tag, TagWorks, and FIDO brand names. Hillman Solutions Corp. is headquartered in Cincinnati, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jon Michael Adinolfi | President, CEO & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $389K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $9K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Hillman Solutions Corp. is a small-cap industrials business with a $1.6B market cap on $1.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $35M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.61\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 2.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.8%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 211% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.1102948511778066},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (80% sell ratio) over the past year","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.2},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 52/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (35% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Financial quality scores above most Industrials peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Hillman Solutions (HLMN) Stock Price Lags Record Q3 Results And Thin Margins","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nasdaq-hlmn/hillman-solutions/news/hillman-solutions-hlmn-stock-price-lags-record-q3-results-an","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793752235.739,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Hillman Solutions Corp (HLMN) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Highlights: Record $457. ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/hillman-solutions-corp-hlmn-q3-210750852.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793740070.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.34,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Hillman (HLMN) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"fool.com","link":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/11/03/hillman-hlmn-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/?source=iedfolrf0000001","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793737012.0,"ori